  "caption": "How to use the atlas in your study group.\n\n1. Share a place. Every place has its own link, so everyone opens the same map.\n2. Compare two crus at the same scale.\n3. Keep notes per place and tag them by course.\n4. Save the places you study.\n5. Find any producer and see where its wines are made.\n\nHow does your group study: in person, online or both? Tell us in the comments.\n\nYesterday's story: B. Central Otago, inland among mountains, is New Zealand's only region with a continental climate.\n\nFree to try. Link in bio. openwineatlas.com\n\n#openwineatlas #winestudy #wset #studygroup #sommelier #winemap #wset3",
